    "tenYearAvg": 100368426,
    "note": "Spider-Man: Brand New Day held #1 for a third straight weekend, dropping 51% to an estimated $70.0M and pushing its 17-day domestic cume to $785.8M — while its worldwide total crossed $2 billion, the second-fastest film ever to do so after Avengers: Endgame. Two dinosaur-themed newcomers opened almost neck-and-neck: Warner Bros.' The End of Oak Street bowed to an estimated $21.0M from 3,446 theaters (86% on Rotten Tomatoes, B CinemaScore), narrowly ahead of Paramount's PAW Patrol: The Dino Movie, which opened to $20.5M from 3,545 theaters (86% RT, A CinemaScore) — Boxoffice Pro flagged that the order between the two could still flip once Monday actuals land. The Odyssey continued its remarkable run, adding $23.2M in its 5th weekend to cross the $500M domestic mark. Angel Studios' Reagan-Gorbachev drama The Brink of War opened softer than hoped at $2.68M from 2,083 theaters despite an A CinemaScore. The overall frame landed at roughly $155.8M, a steep comedown from last weekend's $205.6M, but still running about 72% ahead of the same weekend last year ($90.7M) and 55% above the 10-year average for the slot ($100.4M). These are Sunday estimates; Monday actuals may shift the Oak Street/PAW Patrol order and other figures slightly.",
    "noteHtml": null
  },
