      "rtCritic": null,
      "metacritic": null,
      "rangeLow": 23000000,
      "rangeHigh": 35000000,
      "analysis": "Insidious: Out of the Further rotates into tracking as the clear frontrunner among next weekend's openers. Box Office Pro's long-range call has it at $25M–$35M, comping to 2018's Insidious: The Last Key ($29.5M) and 2023's The Red Door ($33M) on the high side, with a soft-tracking downside around Chapter 3's $22.6M. Box Office Theory's read (via SlashFilm) is tighter and a touch more conservative at $23M–$28M. Given that split, the range here stays wide rather than splitting the difference. The Quorum's latest eight-week chart (via Puck) has the film at 47% awareness/48% interest — second-highest among August titles — though both metrics have ticked down slightly over the last two reads. It'll be squaring off against Spider-Man: Brand New Day's fourth weekend (likely $25M–$30M on its own), so unseating Spidey for #1 is plausible on the high end of tracking but far from guaranteed. Reviews haven't embargoed yet. Theater count is a preliminary estimate pending confirmation.",
