      "analysis": "Jason Statham and Lionsgate reunite for Mutiny, a modest counter-programmer rotating in for Aug 21-23. Box Office Pro's long-range forecast has it at $8M–$12M, squarely within Statham's typical $5M–$15M opening band (The Beekeeper $16.5M, A Working Man $15.5M on the high side; Shelter's recent $5.3M underperformance on the low side). Box Office Theory's take is a shade softer at $6M–$11M, so the range here is kept wide to reflect both reads rather than splitting them. Director Jean-François Richet's prior Lionsgate actioner Plane (also with a proven action lead) opened to $10.2M, a reasonable ceiling comp. No reviews yet. Theater count is a preliminary estimate pending confirmation.",
